        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "We human beings make friends with each other, but it’s not just us. Different animals can also become good friends. Tanja Brandt, a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "falconer",
            "zh": "训隼者"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "shared",
            "ref": "v-share"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "friendship",
            "ref": "v-friendship"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " story of her pet dog and a little owl."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Poldi, the owl, met the dog, Ingo, when Brandt "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "adopted",
            "ref": "v-adopt"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the owl and brought him home. A friendship soon started between the two animals. They enjoy taking walks together. Sometimes they sit comfortably in the grass as the owl rubs his body against the dog’s face. And when the owl wants "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "attention",
            "ref": "v-attention"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", he might give Ingo a quick bite on the ear."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Though he is small, the bird often acts as Ingo’s bodyguard. Once, they were on a walk in the forest with Brandt. There was another owl "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "shrieking",
            "zh": "尖叫"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " above their heads. Poldi then shrieked right back at it. “It was as if he were saying, ‘"
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "Back off",
            "ref": "v-back-off"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " from my friend’,” Brandt explained. According to Brandt, “Poldi may have been smaller, but he was the boss.”"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
